::: {.doc-subject}

List every minimum-cost edit path that transforms this graph into another.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L53515-L53690){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}
```pythonsignature
Graph.optimal_edit_paths(
    other,
    node_match=None,
    edge_match=None,
    node_subst_cost=None,
    node_del_cost=None,
    node_ins_cost=None,
    edge_subst_cost=None,
    edge_del_cost=None,
    edge_ins_cost=None,
    upper_bound=None,
)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

![Optimal edit paths](../assets/graphs/optimal-edit-paths.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt="A three-node path A–B–C beside a triangle X, Y, Z. The first of the six optimal edit paths, each costing 1, maps A to X, B to Y and C to Z (matching colors in both graphs and the card); the path's two edges land on X–Y and Y–Z, and the triangle's third edge Z–X, dashed in accent, is the one insertion." width="100%"}

An edit path is a complete account of how this graph turns into a graph isomorphic to
`other=`: every node of this graph is substituted by a node of `other=` or deleted, every
node of `other=` not substituted is inserted, and the same holds for edges. The cost of
the cheapest path is the exact graph edit distance, the value returned by
`graph_edit_distance(exact=True)`; this method also returns the paths themselves, all of
them when several reach the minimum. For isomorphic graphs the cost is `0` and the paths
are the isomorphisms between the two graphs.

Edit paths are useful to:

- explain a graph edit distance, by showing which nodes and edges correspond
- align two small networks (molecules, workflows, circuits) node by node
- enumerate the different ways two structures can be matched at the same cost

The search is exponential in the worst case and is practical for graphs of up to about a
dozen nodes. Labels play no part, and the current selection is ignored.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[other]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The target graph. It must have the same directedness as the calling graph.

<code>[node_match]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], bool]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Functions called with two attribute dictionaries (a node or edge of this graph and
    one of `other=`), returning `True` when the two may be substituted for free. An edge's
    dictionary holds its attributes plus its `"weight"` when it has one. See
    `graph_edit_distance()`.

<code>[edge_match]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], bool]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Functions called with two attribute dictionaries (a node or edge of this graph and
    one of `other=`), returning `True` when the two may be substituted for free. An edge's
    dictionary holds its attributes plus its `"weight"` when it has one. See
    `graph_edit_distance()`.

<code>[node_subst_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Functions returning the cost of substituting, deleting, and inserting a node. By
    default a substitution costs `0` (or `1` for nodes that fail `node_match=`), and a
    deletion or insertion costs `1`.

<code>[node_del_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Functions returning the cost of substituting, deleting, and inserting a node. By
    default a substitution costs `0` (or `1` for nodes that fail `node_match=`), and a
    deletion or insertion costs `1`.

<code>[node_ins_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Functions returning the cost of substituting, deleting, and inserting a node. By
    default a substitution costs `0` (or `1` for nodes that fail `node_match=`), and a
    deletion or insertion costs `1`.

<code>[edge_subst_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The same three functions for edges, with the same defaults.

<code>[edge_del_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

